RayCAD patch to OCCT 8.0.1 (LGPL-2.1 with the OCCT exception; this file is under the same terms).

What: a cancel reaches two more geometric searches that a boolean or a feature removal can spend minutes in.
  - Message_ProgressIndicator gets a per-thread "current range" (ThreadRange, SetThreadRange, ThreadUserBreak and the
    scope helper ThreadRangeScope), for searches deep in TKGeomAlgo whose interfaces take no progress range.
  - BOPAlgo_EdgeFace and BOPAlgo_FaceFace (the edge/face and face/face jobs of BOPAlgo_PaveFiller) set their job's
    range as the thread's range while they run.
  - IntCurveSurface_InterUtils (the curve/surface intersection under IntTools_BeanFaceIntersector) checks it between
    the passes of its start-point sort and between start points; IntWalk_PWalking (the surface/surface walk under
    IntTools_FaceFace) checks it in its marching loop and while extending a line through a tangent zone. On a break
    they stop: the sort and the search return, the walk returns not done.

Why: RayCAD runs direct edits on a kernel thread it abandons on cancel and requires the abandoned OCCT work to stop
within 10 s (task T-080). On the NIST test models (tests/corpus/directedit/set_nist.tsv) edits ran on long after a
cancel: resizing a hole of NIST CTC 02 (AP203 with PMI) 161 and 167 s, removing a blend run of it 80 s (inside the
PaveFiller of BOPAlgo_MakerVolume), removing a hole stack of NIST D2MI 827-9999-904 40 s on Linux. gdb stack samples
taken while the abandoned thread ran showed one edge/face job inside IntCurveSurface_HInter::Perform
(IntCurveSurface_InterUtils::SortStartPoints, a bubble sort, and ProcessSortedPoints) and one face/face job inside
IntWalk_PWalking::Perform / ExtendLineInCommonZone, each for minutes; patch 0011 made jobs stop only between such
calls. A broken job's partial result is never used: BOPAlgo_PaveFiller checks the break after its jobs and the
operation ends with BOPAlgo_AlertUserBreak. A run that is not cancelled is unchanged (nothing but the break is read).

Upstream: not reported.

diff --git a/src/FoundationClasses/TKernel/Message/Message_ProgressIndicator.cxx b/src/FoundationClasses/TKernel/Message/Message_ProgressIndicator.cxx
--- a/src/FoundationClasses/TKernel/Message/Message_ProgressIndicator.cxx
+++ b/src/FoundationClasses/TKernel/Message/Message_ProgressIndicator.cxx
@@ -15,6 +15,36 @@
 
 IMPLEMENT_STANDARD_RTTIEXT(Message_ProgressIndicator, Standard_Transient)
 
+namespace
+{
+// RayCAD (patch 0012): see Message_ProgressIndicator::ThreadRange().
+thread_local const Message_ProgressRange* THE_THREAD_RANGE = nullptr;
+} // namespace
+
+//=================================================================================================
+
+const Message_ProgressRange* Message_ProgressIndicator::ThreadRange()
+{
+  return THE_THREAD_RANGE;
+}
+
+//=================================================================================================
+
+const Message_ProgressRange* Message_ProgressIndicator::SetThreadRange(
+  const Message_ProgressRange* theRange)
+{
+  const Message_ProgressRange* aPrevious = THE_THREAD_RANGE;
+  THE_THREAD_RANGE                       = theRange;
+  return aPrevious;
+}
+
+//=================================================================================================
+
+bool Message_ProgressIndicator::ThreadUserBreak()
+{
+  return THE_THREAD_RANGE != nullptr && THE_THREAD_RANGE->UserBreak();
+}
+
 //=================================================================================================
 
 Message_ProgressIndicator::Message_ProgressIndicator()
diff --git a/src/FoundationClasses/TKernel/Message/Message_ProgressIndicator.hxx b/src/FoundationClasses/TKernel/Message/Message_ProgressIndicator.hxx
--- a/src/FoundationClasses/TKernel/Message/Message_ProgressIndicator.hxx
+++ b/src/FoundationClasses/TKernel/Message/Message_ProgressIndicator.hxx
@@ -74,6 +74,31 @@ public:
   Standard_EXPORT static Message_ProgressRange Start(
     const occ::handle<Message_ProgressIndicator>& theProgress);
 
+  //!@name RayCAD (patch 0012): a user break for long geometric searches that take no progress range
+  //! The range whose user break the calling thread's long geometric searches poll (the start points of a
+  //! curve/surface intersection, a surface/surface walk), or null. Set by the jobs of a boolean that own a range.
+  Standard_EXPORT static const Message_ProgressRange* ThreadRange();
+  //! Sets the calling thread's range (null: none) and returns the previous one, to be restored.
+  Standard_EXPORT static const Message_ProgressRange* SetThreadRange(const Message_ProgressRange* theRange);
+  //! True if the calling thread has a range and its indicator signals a user break.
+  Standard_EXPORT static bool ThreadUserBreak();
+
+  //! Sets the calling thread's range for its lifetime and restores the previous one after.
+  class ThreadRangeScope
+  {
+  public:
+    explicit ThreadRangeScope(const Message_ProgressRange& theRange)
+        : myPrevious(SetThreadRange(&theRange))
+    {
+    }
+    ~ThreadRangeScope() { SetThreadRange(myPrevious); }
+    ThreadRangeScope(const ThreadRangeScope&)            = delete;
+    ThreadRangeScope& operator=(const ThreadRangeScope&) = delete;
+
+  private:
+    const Message_ProgressRange* myPrevious;
+  };
+
 protected:
   //!@name Virtual methods to be defined by descendant.
 
